#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:84
#: cdf2b29ac85c43a6a099fb17ab4423ed
msgid "The BLITZ Whoop F7 AIO has 4 PWM outputs internally connected to its 4-in-1 ESC. The pads for motor output are M1 to M4 on the board. All 4 outputs support bi-directional DShot and DShot, as well as all PWM types. The default configuration is for bi-directional DShot using the already installed BlueJay firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:86
#: 046885fac9554ec9b6525e7dd4ff02b7
msgid "The PWM are in in two groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:88
#: 7ee46d78ab644bebbc0ebba9241db01a
msgid "PWM 1-4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:89
#: 9790f27aa6834674842c60d2ce2fd7b7
msgid "PWM 5 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:91
#: 7db6a14863114eef9300f157a081086f
msgid "for users migrating from BetaflightX quads, the first four outputs M1-M4 have been configured for use with existing motor wiring using these default parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:93
#: 5f24090a340149cd8252704157ae64e0
msgid ":ref:`FRAME_CLASS<FRAME_CLASS>` = 1 (Quad)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:94
#: bb346d1dea1d490c8935370f4165a001
msgid ":ref:`FRAME_TYPE<FRAME_TYPE>` = 12 (BetaFlightX)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:98
#: 80f08ee9486f445c96102ffc2243a37c
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:100
#: d24ea6e927624b0083791933e44a41b2
msgid "RC input is configured by default on RX2 on the DJI connector and supports all single wire RC protocols (SBUS,DSM,etc.) except PPM. FPort, when connected in this manner, can provide RC but without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:102
#: 151ea672f1e840dea11e49c17c1f4c67
msgid "CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2  require a full UART connection. You should use one with DMA for CRSF/ELRS. For example you could retask UART4 for GPS by setting :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL<SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = \"5\" (GPS), then use UART3 for RC input and set :ref:`SERIAL3_PROTOCOL<SERIAL3_PROTOCOL>` = \"23\". Under this scenario:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:104
#: ec481615976e42a3b5d8a5dbd41b0965
msgid "CRSF also requires a TX3 connection, in addition to RX3, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:106
#: 7c77c58ff5494cef94ece73d03d1968c
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX3 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL3_OPTIONS<SERIAL3_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:108
#: 448f352ab50c404a8c6772fba2f3a79d
msgid "FPORT with telemetry could use this setup also, but connects only to TX3 and :ref:`SERIAL3_OPTIONS<SERIAL3_OPTIONS>` would be set to \"7\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:111
#: 8a34ba0963ea4de393ad6cb8704bd6ef
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-blitzf7AIO.rst:113
#: e6c2fa4728ca4493bafd8a9759432d40
msgid "The Blitz Whoop F7 AIO supports analog video transmission using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort is supported by default on USART1 RX/TX or any other free UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

